      "side": 1,
      "message": "I notice data reset is not configured in few more boards(boldar/volteer/terrador/primus/ anahera/kano/copano/felwinter) which has CONFIG_USB_PD_USB4  as enabled. \nHow about enabling it by default in config.h itself based on CONFIG_USB_PD_USB4  \u0026 remove direct configuration from  brya \u0026 brask based boardfiles?\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_USB_PD_USB4\n#define CONFIG_USB_PD_DATA_RESET_MSG\n#endif",
      "parentUuid": "46c1b2bd_7893dcf6",
      "revId": "d9156cf57ecc1bb11f1790ac70eab3f8e270734e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f617b4b_c6be346d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365384
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T06:50:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Abe! Seems like  data reset Config doesn\u0027t get enabled, if enabled in config.h based on condition, because board file where CONFIG_USB_PD_USB4 is enabled gets compiled after common config file is  done and hence don\u0027t see the config - CONFIG_USB_PD_USB4  and hence  CONFIG_USB_PD_DATA_RESET_MSG  is not getting enabled. So we have to go with this way of enabling specifically in board file itself, as of now.",
      "parentUuid": "64ab42dd_21424f8b",
      "revId": "d9156cf57ecc1bb11f1790ac70eab3f8e270734e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
